  "title": "Agent tooling: Pages publish waits for its deploy, plus check:changed and worktree setup",
  "body": "A retro of the last 10 agent sessions found agents losing time on the same repo tooling gaps: Pages deploys that 404 for minutes after a \"successful\" publish, worktrees without `node_modules`/`.env`, hand-built `vp check` file lists that break in zsh, and AGENTS.md pointers that lead to the wrong files or commands.\n\n- **Pages publish waits for its deploy.** `scripts/pages-review.ts publish` now waits for the `pages-build-deployment` run whose `head_sha` is the pushed `gh-pages` commit, reruns it once if it fails (the usual \"in progress deployment\" lock), and prints `deploy <state>` after the URL. `--no-wait` skips it. The pages skill now says a 404 means the deploy is running or failed, what to do on a lasting lock, and to publish once per PR with screenshots inside the export folder.\n- **`pnpm check:changed`** runs `vp check --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern` on files changed against the merge-base with `origin/main` plus untracked files. Markdown-only lists no longer fail with \"No files found to lint\". Extra flags pass through (`--fix`).\n- **`node scripts/setup-worktree.ts`** works outside T3: without `T3CODE_PROJECT_ROOT`, it links `.env` from the main checkout (first `git worktree list` entry).\n- **AGENTS.md** points to `pnpm ui:screenshots`, `src/api/`, real `src/review/` file names, how to find every layer for a new review field, `pnpm generate:schema` / `pnpm sync:skill` before commit, the `skills-next` + local-CLI PR review flow, and `--cli-login`.\n\nComprehende review: https://matemolnar8.github.io/comprehende/pr/182/ (published with the new wait: `deploy success` after 59 s)\n\nVerified: `vp test run scripts/pages-review.test.ts scripts/setup-worktree.test.ts` (16 passed), `pnpm check:changed` clean, `node scripts/setup-worktree.ts` without the env var in this worktree linked `.env`. No smoke eval: nothing under `skills-next/comprehende/`, `src/schema/`, or `src/review/` changed.\n\nCreated with Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code.\n",
